      "notes": "All claims check out against cited evidence. The E3 quote is from The Guardian reporting government statements \u2014 the claim correctly characterises it as 'the scale of financial exposure this policy addresses' rather than asserting it as a measured fact, which is acceptable. E20 ('Many mid-rise and low-rise buildings remain untouched') is sourced only from britsafe.org, a single media/advocacy-adjacent source, but is used as a supporting caveat rather than a verdict-driving claim, so warrants only a warning. The direction 'improves' is well-supported by the legal protections already in force (E1, E11). Magnitude 'moderate' is appropriately justified by scope gaps and slow pace. No tier blurring, no party identity leakage, no false balance issues \u2014 the direction is unambiguous and no spurious counter-claims are introduced."
